    "summary": "Goal: no secret-like value given on the command line as a check name, agent name or session id is written to any task record or the ACTIVE pointer; the command refuses before it runs anything or writes anything. Reproduced with a synthetic token on the current engine and on the pinned v1.0.0: run with such a check id or agent name writes it into the verification.md check block, then save_state refuses state.json; resume, preflight and new with such an agent name write it into ACTIVE (git-ignored but on disk) before the refusal, and new also leaves a task folder without state.json that blocks the name; a secret-like --session is written into ACTIVE and the command succeeds. Affected: api.py (entry validation, run_check order), store/state.py, tests. Out of scope: TD-24, TD-26, approve snapshotting an unscanned spec or plan, refusal messages that echo inputs to the terminal, check ids with | or newlines, the Claude hook's session from its own payload."
  },
